<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates softer to steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates softer to steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were softer to steady on Tuesday in line with the decline in Treasury bill rates at the latest auction, traders said.</p>
<p>The one-week, two-week, six-month and one-year rates were lower, while the rest were steady.</p>
<p>Traders also said the market is flooded with cash from maturing floating rate treasury notes amounting to about 5.0 billion pesos.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  Feb 25		 FEB 24</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  5/16		10  3/8</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		26-Feb		  25-Feb</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
